# AgentRec-X - real-provider (DeepSeek) configuration - EXAMPLE ONLY.
#
#   1. copy this file to `.env`   (`.env` and `.env.*` are git-ignored)
#   2. fill in the credential below
#   3. `docker compose up`
#
# Do NOT commit a filled-in copy. This file holds no credential.
#
# Offline is the default: with `AGENTRECX_AGENT_POLICY` unset (or `deterministic`), the
# container unsets every AGENTRECX_LLM_* variable at startup and makes no network call.

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# Two independent LLM switches - do not conflate them
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# (1) `AGENTRECX_AGENT_POLICY=llm` selects the CONTROL-PLANE model policy for the single-turn
#     POST /v1/demo/agent/recommend endpoint (the bounded agent loop).  Under
#     `docker compose` this switch is ALSO what keeps the AGENTRECX_LLM_* variables:
#     scripts/entrypoint.sh unsets them unless the policy is `llm`.  The bare-metal
#     ./scripts/start_demo.sh passes the environment through unchanged.
#
# (2) The browser demo's Decision Mode (`Deterministic` | `LLM Agent`) selects its decision
#     policy per session in the page.  **Deterministic is the DEFAULT** and needs nothing from
#     this file: no provider, no credential, no network.  The optional `LLM Agent` mode needs
#     the four AGENTRECX_LLM_* values below and nothing else - it does not need switch (1),
#     which only affects the endpoint above.
#
#     In that mode the model may propose exactly two things: the route, and which stated
#     preference values are stored or withdrawn.  Candidates, product identity, scores,
#     evidence, whether a mutation was actually applied, and the final ranking remain owned by
#     trusted code, and the plan schema has no field that could carry them.
#
# Do NOT set `AGENTRECX_CONTROL_PLANE=loop` for a browser LLM-mode acceptance run: the
# browser's LLM mode composes the accepted graph path and reports itself unavailable under a
# loop control plane.
AGENTRECX_AGENT_POLICY=llm

# --- provider (shared by both switches) ------------------------------------- #
AGENTRECX_LLM_BASE_URL=https://api.deepseek.com/v1
AGENTRECX_LLM_MODEL=deepseek-flash

# A named provider protocol profile (see recommendation/control/provider_adapter.py).
# `deepseek` sends response_format={"type":"json_object"} plus thinking disabled, and is the
# name the Recommendation Trace reports as the provider.
AGENTRECX_LLM_PROFILE=deepseek

# Your credential. Passed only as an environment variable at run time; never baked into the
# image, never logged, never written to a result artifact.  Leave it empty in this file and
# supply it at run time (see docs/USAGE.md).
AGENTRECX_LLM_API_KEY=
